# plant-qos1 — a fleet of power plants. Each site's bridge is ONE publisher connection
# carrying that site's own 250 topics (`<prefix>/<site>/<tag>`: mqtt-load --bridge
# --topics-per-connection), payloads of 50 to 200 bytes, and one durable `$share` group
# shares every topic (mqtt-load --shape share-all), as a historian takes the whole
# fleet's data. Durable QoS 1, no retain.
#
# Sites follow the rate: a step's sites on a generator are its rate ÷ RATE_PER_PUBLISHER,
# rounded up to a whole number per broker, so every broker carries as many sites and a
# site carries at most 10,000 msg/s. That holds on every tier, h3's fixed 20,000 clients
# included (DEF_PUBLISHERS below).
#
# CONSUMERS is the group's members per generator, dealt evenly over the brokers. 240
# keeps a member under 1,100 msg/s at 1,000,000 msg/s on 10 brokers and 4 generators,
# well under one durable session's ceiling of about 2,500 (#1134).
#
# Each site keeps up to INFLIGHT publishes in flight, capped by the broker's Receive
# Maximum: 256 unless raised, which holds a site at 256 ÷ the ack latency. Run with
# EXTRA_BROKER_ENV="MQTTD_RECEIVE_MAXIMUM=4096" to use the 4,096 below. At 4,096, 16 sites
# on one broker can fill its table of 65,536 publishes waiting for their acks.
#
# Values here are defaults: anything exported in the environment wins.
QOS=${QOS:-1}
SHAPE=${SHAPE:-share-all}
SESSIONS=${SESSIONS:-durable}
SESSION_EXPIRY=${SESSION_EXPIRY:-30}
PAYLOAD=${PAYLOAD:-50-200}
# A site's topics. mqtt-load counts the run's topics as sites × TOPICS_PER_CONNECTION;
# TOPICS only labels the ladder.
TOPICS_PER_CONNECTION=${TOPICS_PER_CONNECTION:-250}
TOPICS=${TOPICS:-$TOPICS_PER_CONNECTION}
CONSUMERS=${CONSUMERS:-240}
SHARE_GROUPS=${SHARE_GROUPS:-1}
BRIDGE=${BRIDGE:-1}
RATE_PER_PUBLISHER=${RATE_PER_PUBLISHER:-10000}
# Sites follow the rate on every tier: no fixed publisher count.
DEF_PUBLISHERS=
INFLIGHT=${INFLIGHT:-4096}
LATENCY_GATE=${LATENCY_GATE:-ack}
START_RATE_local=${START_RATE_local:-3000}
START_RATE_n3=${START_RATE_n3:-60000}
START_RATE_n10=${START_RATE_n10:-200000}
START_RATE_h3=${START_RATE_h3:-150000}
